# Avalanche L1 failover-benchmark configuration.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Everything is driven from a single CONTROL HOST: it runs the orchestration
# scripts, the load generator (bombard), and the Prometheus/Grafana monitoring
# stack. The control host never runs an L1 node itself, so it survives a full
# site outage and keeps recording the survivors.

# Anchor network: fuji (default) or mainnet. The usual selector is the
# --mainnet flag on the setup scripts (01_fund_wallet.sh, 02_create_chain.sh);
# setting AVALANCHE_NETWORK here does the same for every command without the
# flag. NETWORK= is accepted as an alias. Once the chain is created its network
# is pinned in network.env and wins over this.
#   AVALANCHE_NETWORK=fuji

# NOTE: the kit binaries (bin/l1, bin/fuji-wallet, ...) load THIS .env and
# network.env relative to the binary (bin/..) or the current directory. Run
# them from the kit root (or via the setup/run scripts); invoked from an
# unrelated directory with a relocated binary they cannot find .env and will
# silently drop API_TOKEN / PCHAIN_API (429 risk on the public API).

# SSH user for every node (all nodes share one user).
SSH_USER=ubuntu

# Path on the control host to the SSH private key that reaches every node.
# All nodes must accept this key. Required, no default.
SSH_KEY_PATH=/home/ubuntu/.ssh/your-fleet-key

# =============================================================================
# TOPOLOGY - nodes.ini
# =============================================================================
# The fleet inventory does NOT live here: it is nodes.ini, next to this file
# (cp nodes.ini.example nodes.ini, then set host= to your machines). One line
# per node:
#
#   <name> host=<ip> role=validator|rpc [dc=<tag>]
#
# The node name is the primary key everywhere (fleet verbs, staking/l1/<name>
# key dirs, data/<name> on the boxes). role=validator nodes are registered as
# L1 validators at `l1 create`, all at weight 1000; real weights are on-chain
# state only, moved with `l1 apply` (a "spare" is just a validator at low
# weight). role=rpc nodes track the chain and serve the load-generator
# ingress, never validate, and never carry a BLS signer key. dc= is a
# display-only grouping tag.
#
# Ports are positional per host (the k-th node on a host serves HTTP on
# 9650+2k, staking on 9651+2k), so several nodes can share a box for tests;
# a box loss then takes all of them, so keep one node per box for a
# production-fidelity DR test. See nodes.ini.example and the README.

# =============================================================================
# FUJI P-CHAIN ANCHORING
# =============================================================================
# The fleet anchors its L1 on a public Avalanche P-chain, Fuji or mainnet
# (partial-sync + p-chain-follow-only on every node; see
# docs/two-site-failover.md).
# Validators must have ZERO external connectivity: in nodes.ini, list them by
# their DC-INTERNAL addresses (a node's host= doubles as its --public-ip).
# Only the RPC machines get ONE outgoing TCP, to the pinned public Fuji peer.
#
# FUJI_UPSTREAM_IPS/IDS: the public Fuji peer the RPC tier's P-chain follows.
# Defaults (in _common.sh) point at the first Fuji entry of the pinned
# avalanchego commit's genesis/bootstrappers.json (Ava Labs-operated; NodeID is
# enforced by the TLS handshake). Only set these to override, e.g. after an
# AVALANCHEGO_COMMIT bump rotated the hardcoded bootstrapper IPs. Keep the RPC
# machines' firewall egress rule in lockstep with this value.
#   FUJI_UPSTREAM_IPS=18.192.93.241:9651
#   FUJI_UPSTREAM_IDS=NodeID-2m38qc95mhHXtrhjyGbe7r2NhniqHHJRB
#
# PCHAIN_API: public API used by bin/l1 (chain creation, weight moves),
# fuji-wallet (funding, top-ups) and the fleet's read-only status/exporter
# weight reads. The follow-only RPC tier can never serve platform.* calls, so
# everything P-chain goes here. There is no C-chain dependency at all: weight
# changes are self-signed warp messages submitted straight to the P-chain.
# Default: https://api.avax-test.network
#   PCHAIN_API=https://api.avax-test.network
#
# API_TOKEN: optional rate-limit-bypass token for the public API. When set,
# every P-chain/info request carries it as a token=<value> query param
# (Cloudflare bypass rule on api.avax.network). Unset: nothing changes. The
# value is a secret: keep it in this gitignored .env only, never commit it.
#   API_TOKEN=
